    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing our highest floor, boasting an elite 71.62 score. His combination of a favorable 4.12 xERA matchup against Martin and his sustained 0.452 xwOBA makes him the anchor of our lineup. Following closely, **Trea Turner** (66.93) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (66.29) are high-priority starts. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is particularly intriguing; despite facing a difficult 2.19 xERA arm in Misiorowski, his aggressive slotting in the leadoff spot and a 14% boost from dynamic platoon metrics make him a vital asset for our scarcest category, stolen bases. Similarly, **Lars Nootbaar** capitalizes on a soft 4.42 xERA matchup against Painter, with platoon and order advantages pushing his score to a strong 65.16.\n\nOur primary bench decision centered on **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, who possesses strong underlying metrics, including a massive 14% park factor and 19% SP skill boost, but was ultimately excluded due to his status outside the starting lineup. On the active roster, **Carson Benge** represents our most volatile start; while he is currently slotted at 45.29, his score is severely depressed by a -12% SP skill penalty against Jax. We are monitoring **Gary Sanchez** (58.94) closely, as his moderate score is buoyed by favorable wind conditions (+5%) and a decent 4.24 xERA matchup against Peterson, D. Conversely, **Caleb Durbin** faces a high-risk environment with -5% wind pressure, though his elite speed profile keeps him in the mix as a necessary SB contributor. We remain cautious regarding **Junior Caminero**, whose 49.83 score is suffering from a -19% SP skill penalty; he remains a marginal start, prioritized only to maintain our Roto production targets.",
